@title FW-482: average four humidity reads, sample every 2 s
@subtitle Fixes false 100% humidity alarms and roughly halves average current

## Why this change exists

Three units in a Lisbon warehouse raised false 100% humidity alarms. A glitched read returned 0xFFFF, and the old code converted it straight to 100 %RH and reported it as real.

Battery life is the second problem. In the field it is only about 14 months, because the sensor is sampled every 500 ms and draws 212 µA on average.

## What changed

- `humidity_read()` now takes 4 reads and reports their average, not a single read.
- Any read that returns 0xFFFF aborts the whole sample and returns `-EIO`. No value is written to `*out`.
- `wdt_feed()` is called after each read. Four reads take about 150 ms and the watchdog timeout is 1 s, so the loop stays well inside it.
- `SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS` goes from 500 to 2000, which is where most of the current saving comes from.

## Bench results

kpi Average current | 96 µA | -55% from 212 µA | good
kpi Noise | ±0.6 %RH | down from ±1.8 %RH | good
kpi Worst alarm delay | 2 s | up from 0.5 s | bad

If average current were the only drain, 96 µA against 212 µA would stretch the 14 months to roughly 31 months. That is arithmetic, not a field measurement.

## Risk

!! Alarms can now be detected up to 2 s late, up from 0.5 s. Product's limit is 5 s, so the margin is 3 s.

!! Not tested below -10 °C. The bench results do not cover cold-storage conditions.

## For reviewers

- [ ] Check what the caller of `humidity_read()` does with `-EIO`. It must not raise an alarm and must not use a stale or zero value. Before this change the function always returned 0, so this path is new.
- [ ] A sensor stuck at 0xFFFF now produces no readings at all rather than a false 100%. Confirm that is the behaviour we want, or whether repeated `-EIO` should raise a fault.
- [ ] One bad read throws away all four. There is no retry inside the function.
- [ ] `sum / SAMPLES_PER_AVG` is integer division. The truncation is under 1 raw count, about 0.0015 %RH, so I left it.

## Diff

```diff
--- a/src/sensor/humidity.c
+++ b/src/sensor/humidity.c
@@ -41,14 +41,22 @@
-#define SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS 500
+#define SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS 2000
+#define SAMPLES_PER_AVG  4

 int humidity_read(float *out)
 {
-    uint16_t raw = read_raw();
-    *out = raw * 100.0f / 65535.0f;
-    return 0;
+    uint32_t sum = 0;
+    for (int i = 0; i < SAMPLES_PER_AVG; i++) {
+        uint16_t raw = read_raw();
+        if (raw == 0xFFFF) {
+            return -EIO;
+        }
+        sum += raw;
+        wdt_feed();
+    }
+    *out = (sum / SAMPLES_PER_AVG) * 100.0f / 65535.0f;
+    return 0;
 }
```

Ticket: FW-482
